  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xe4;dda Barnen &#x2013; Social sammanh&#xe5;llning, fredsbyggande och motst&#xe5;ndskraft 2021&#x2013;2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children - Social Cohesion, Peace Building and Resiliency 2021-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen &#xe4;mnar f&#xf6;rbr&#xe4;ttra lokala samh&#xe4;llen sociala sammanh&#xe5;llning, v&#xe4;lm&#xe5;ende och f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att &#xe5;terintegrera utsatta pojkar och flickor som riskerar att associeras eller som har anknytning till v&#xe4;pnade grupper genom tillhandah&#xe5;llandet av sociala skyddsn&#xe4;t, utbildning, f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning samt civil-milit&#xe4;r koordinering.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention aims to improve the social cohesion, well-being and capacity of local communities to reintegrate vulnerable boys and girls at risk of association or associated with armed groups through the provision of social protection, education, livelihoods and civil-military coordination.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the program is to improve community level social cohesion, well-being and reintegration of vulnerable boys and  girls at risk or associated with armed groups through integrated gender responsive, disability inclusive child protection, livelihood (CVA) and education services

The proposed program will achieve the following four key results:

Result 1. Vulnerable boys and girls affected by conflict and insecurity improve their safety and well-being through better, more equitable and inclusive access to comprehensive and conflict-sensitive child protection services.

Result 2. Vulnerable IDP and host community households are resilient and meet their basic needs through improved access to economic, food, life skills and community capacity building opportunities.

Result 3. Children (girls and boys) from communities affected by the security crisis have access to inclusive quality education in a safe and protective environment through capacity building in emergency education and psychological first aid.

Result 4. Community cohesion, child protection practice, and civil-military coordination is increased in order to facilitate programmes and protection of children and civilians affected by armed conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
